@*
    The everyday mode, and the one with nothing to configure: it reads the smoothed surplus and sets
    the current the sun can cover, once the home battery is full. Everything it decides on is already
    a live figure, so the tab is a button and the three numbers that say whether pressing it would
    achieve anything right now.
*@

<p class="muted">
    Charge from whatever the roof is making that the house is not already using. The home battery
    keeps first claim: this mode waits until the battery is full, then follows the surplus up and
    down, and pauses when there is not enough of it to hold the charger's minimum current.
</p>

<div class="control">
    <button type="button" class="primary" id="start-solar" disabled="@Busy" @onclick="StartSolar">
        Charge from surplus
    </button>
    <span class="hint">
        Puts the charger into Fast and hands it to the surplus. Nothing else to set — the current is
        whatever the sun leaves over, decided again every poll.
    </span>
</div>

@if (Status is { } status)
{
    <section class="stat-grid">
        <Stat Label="Solar surplus" Value="@Watts(status.SurplusWatts)"
              Hint="PV left after household consumption — the smoothed 3-minute average this mode decides on. Blank while a mode that doesn't decide on surplus is driving." />
        <Stat Label="Battery SOC" Value="@Percent(status.BatterySocPercent)"
              Hint="The gate for this mode: the car gets nothing until the home battery is full." />
        <Stat Label="EV charging power" Value="@Watts(status.EvChargerPowerWatts)"
              Hint="What the charger reports the car actually drawing right now — not a setpoint." />
        <Stat Label="Target current" Value="@Amps(status.TargetCurrentAmps)"
              Hint="The current this mode decided on this cycle, before it was written. Blank whenever it isn't charging." />
    </section>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public ChargeControlStatus? Status { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool Busy { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public Func<ChargeControlMode, Task<ChargeActionResult>> Start { get; set; } = default!;

    private Task StartSolar() => Start(ChargeControlMode.Solar);

    private static string Watts(double watts) => $"{watts:F0} W";

    private static string Watts(double? watts) => watts is null ? "—" : $"{watts.Value:F0} W";

    private static string Percent(double percent) => $"{percent:F0}%";

    private static string Amps(int? amps) => amps is null ? "—" : $"{amps.Value} A";
}
